usage: aip-spec validate [-h] skill_dir

Validate an AIP skill folder.

positional arguments:
  skill_dir   path to the skill folder (containing SKILL.md)

options:
  -h, --help  show this help message and exit
usage: aip run [-h] [--input INPUT] [--interactive] [--run-file RUN_FILE]
               [--workdir WORKDIR] [--progress] [--debug]
               skill_dir|name

Run a procedure, pausing when the client must decide: a skill folder runs
locally, a published name runs on the server. Prints one JSON object: paused
or done (exit 0), or error (exit 1); see docs/cli-json.md.

positional arguments:
  skill_dir|name

options:
  -h, --help           show this help message and exit
  --input, -i INPUT    JSON object for the start step; `-` reads stdin
  --interactive        prompt on the terminal instead of pausing to a run file
  --run-file RUN_FILE  where to write the run file (default ~/.aip/runs/<run-
                       id>.json; AIP_HOME moves it)
  --workdir WORKDIR    the run's working directory, where its scripts read and
                       write files (AIP_WORKDIR); recorded in the run file so
                       resume works from anywhere (default the current
                       directory)
  --progress           print one JSON line per completed step before the final
                       object (itself one line)
  --debug              print a traceback on stderr when the run fails

